; ============================================================
; ELIZA for the 1802 — STELLAR   *** MILESTONE 3b: PRONOUN SWAP ***
; ============================================================
; C7 00 (multitasking off) + F0 00 00 pre-pass end marker -> loads into dirty RAM.
; Full core engine: keyword match (FINDKEY) + fragment echo + pronoun swap.
;   "I AM SAD" -> "HOW LONG HAVE YOU BEEN SAD?"
;   "I FEEL YOU HATE MY DOG" -> "DO YOU OFTEN FEEL I HATE YOUR DOG?"
;
; *** TYPE IN CAPITALS *** (auto-upper is a later step).
;
; The $01 marker in a reply splices in the fragment (input after the keyword).
; While copying it, at every space the swap table ($4A00) is checked with a
; trailing-word-boundary test, swapping whole words only:
;   YOU<->I   MY<->YOUR   ARE<->AM   (single left-to-right pass, no re-swap)
;
; NOTE (fixed): the "emit fragment char" path re-reads M(R3) before OUTCH,
; because the swap-table scan clobbers Acc — otherwise a non-swapped space came
; out as a $00 (invisible), giving "BEENSAD" instead of "BEEN SAD".
;
; Memory:
;   $4000..4209  code (ends F0 00 00)
;   $4700..$479A  strings   $4800..4962  keyword table ($01=splice)
;   $4A00..4A36  swap table [FROM\0][TO\0]... (FROM has leading space)
;   $5000..$50FF  INPUT buffer
;
; Keyword table (priority order):
;   HELLO     -> HELLO. HOW ARE YOU FEELING TODAY?
;   COMPUTER  -> DO COMPUTERS WORRY YOU?
;   I FEEL    -> DO YOU OFTEN FEEL ?
;   I AM      -> HOW LONG HAVE YOU BEEN ?
;   I WANT    -> WHY DO YOU WANT ?
;   WHY       -> WHY DO YOU ASK?
;   NAME      -> NAMES DON'T INTEREST ME.
;   DREAM     -> WHAT DOES THAT DREAM SUGGEST TO YOU?
;   SORRY     -> PLEASE DON'T APOLOGIZE.
;   YOU       -> WE WERE DISCUSSING YOU, NOT ME.
;   YES       -> YOU SEEM QUITE CERTAIN.
;   NO        -> WHY NOT?
;   (no match) -> "PLEASE GO ON."
;
; Validated: decodes cleanly $4000..4209; 38 labels, all 54 targets matched.
; ============================================================

